\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let $X$ be a closed oriented Riemannian manifold of strictly positive scalar curvature, and let $\Gamma$ be a discrete group. For every continuous map $f:X\to B\Gamma$, must $f_*[X]=0$ in $H_{\dim X}(B\Gamma;\mathbb Q)$? The classifying space $B\Gamma$ has fundamental group $\Gamma$ and contractible universal cover. The assertion concerns rational homology and includes both spin and nonspin manifolds.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://www.ihes.fr/~gromov/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/101-problemsOct1-2017.pdf}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let $X$ be a closed oriented Riemannian manifold of strictly positive scalar curvature, and let $\Gamma$ be a discrete group. For every continuous map $f:X\to B\Gamma$, must $f_*[X]=0$ in $H_{\dim X}(B\Gamma;\mathbb Q)$? The classifying space $B\Gamma$ has fundamental group $\Gamma$ and contractible universal cover. The assertion concerns rational homology and includes both spin and nonspin manifolds.

